  "description": "The same freshness half for the commonest block of all (spec/execution-model.md:377-379): the second turn of a `repeat` must not find the `:carried` the first turn bound, so the read raises `ol-undefined-var` (spec/error-model.md:102). `repcount` supplies the turn number without needing a binding of its own. The existing `a-fresh-binding-on-every-loop-turn` prints `1 1 1 1` from `repeat 4 [ :x = 0   :x = :x + 1   print :x ]`, which reads like the freshness test but does not discriminate on its own — the `:x = 0` resets a shared frame to exactly the same output — so before this fixture `repeat` freshness was pinned only indirectly, through the handler-capture fixtures. Added at the QA reviewer's request during the review gate.",
